      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbal",
          "text": "Motor vehicle accidents are a leading cause of unintentional injury death in the United States. An early estimate for 2022 from the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sban",
          "text": "National Highway Traffic Safety Administration",
          "marks": [
            "lbam"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbao",
          "text": " states that 42,795 people died in motor vehicle traffic accidents nationwide. Fatal car accidents can happen when a family least expects it and cause immense emotional turmoil. Review the latest available statistics and preliminary data for deadly collisions in Colorado in 2022 to learn more.",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbar",
      "style": "h2",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbaq",
          "text": "How Many People Die in Fatal Collisions in Colorado Each Year?",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbaz",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [
        {
          "_key": "lbat",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "/denver-car-accident-lawyer/"
        },
        {
          "_key": "lbaw",
          "_type": "link",
          "href": "https://www.codot.gov/news/2023/january/745-lives-lost-on-colorado-roads-2022"
        }
      ],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbas",
          "text": "Data shows that in 2022, an estimated 757 people died in fatal ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbau",
          "text": "car accidents",
          "marks": [
            "lbat"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbav",
          "text": " in Colorado. This is a 9.6 percent increase from the fatality rate in 2021 (691 deaths). The death rate per 100 motor vehicle miles traveled was 1.44, up from 1.31 in 2021. According to the ",
          "marks": []
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbax",
          "text": "Colorado Department of Transportation",
          "marks": [
            "lbaw"
          ]
        },
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbay",
          "text": ", 2022’s traffic accident death toll represents a startling 57 percent increase from 10 years ago. It is also the highest death toll in the state since 1981. The counties with the highest numbers of deaths in Colorado in 2022 were:",
          "marks": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "_type": "block",
      "_key": "bbb1",
      "style": "normal",
      "markDefs": [],
      "children": [
        {
          "_type": "span",
          "_key": "sbb0",
          "text": "El Paso: 83",
          "marks": []
        }
      ],
      "listItem": "bullet",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
